From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody McGinnis <brainwart@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:22:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] usb: dwc3: qcom-legacy: drop the required-opps CX vote
 in system suspend

The glue's "required-opps" (nominal on CX) is applied by genpd at attach
and only dropped on runtime suspend. xhci-plat runtime resumes the
controller for system suspend, which resumes the glue too, so the glue
enters s2idle holding CX at nominal even though its clocks and
interconnect votes are off. On SC8280XP that keeps CX from collapsing.

Drop the vote in the system suspend callback and restore the
"required-opps" level on resume, before the clocks come back. Wakeup
interrupts go through the PDC and do not need the CX vote.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
index 189f5447a..908e6da60 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom-legacy.c
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 #include <linux/interconnect.h>
 #include <linux/of_platform.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_domain.h>
+#include <linux/pm_opp.h>
 #include <linux/phy/phy.h>
 #include <linux/usb/of.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
@@ -872,6 +874,14 @@ static int __maybe_unused dwc3_qcom_pm_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The "required-opps" vote on the GDSC's parent (CX) is applied at
+	 * attach and only dropped by genpd on runtime suspend. The controller
+	 * is runtime resumed for system suspend (xhci-plat), so drop it here;
+	 * wakeup detection does not need it.
+	 */
+	dev_pm_genpd_set_performance_state(dev, 0);
+
 	qcom->pm_suspended = true;
 
 	return 0;
@@ -881,8 +891,16 @@ static int __maybe_unused dwc3_qcom_pm_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct dwc3_qcom *qcom = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	bool wakeup = device_may_wakeup(dev);
+	int pstate;
 	int ret;
 
+	pstate = of_get_required_opp_performance_state(dev->of_node, 0);
+	if (pstate > 0) {
+		ret = dev_pm_genpd_set_performance_state(dev, pstate);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	ret = dwc3_qcom_resume(qcom, wakeup);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
